    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite (only `AcceptanceTest` exists) is green: 3 tests, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented optional, region-validated `postcode` on owner creation with minimal structural impact \u2014 no complex method was grown; the logic lives in a new small cohesive class.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `postcode` property to `OwnerFields` with `pattern: ^\\d{4}$`. Bean Validation rejects malformed (non-4-digit) postcodes with 400, and it's absent from `required` so the request contract stays backward-compatible. Regenerating the DTO gives `OwnerDto` the field so it's returned in JSON.\n2. **`PostcodeValidator.java`** (new) \u2014 `validate(city, postcode)` returns the postcode when absent or in range, else throws `IllegalArgumentException` (mapped to 400 by the existing advice). It reuses `LocalityResolver` for the city\u2192region lookup and holds the fixed region ranges (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099); an unknown region accepts any 4-digit value.\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `postcode` field with a plain getter/setter (`@Column(name=\"postcode\")`), so it persists and is mapped back.\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` line routing `postcode` through `PostcodeValidator.validate(city, postcode)` during `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)`.\n5. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql` / `data.sql`** \u2014 added the `postcode` column (appended last) and a trailing `NULL` to the positional seed inserts. The h2 dev profile uses `ddl-auto=update`, so it needs no schema edit.\n\nOnly the abstract mapper method got a single added annotation line; the validation lives in a brand-new class with near-zero surrounding complexity, keeping WMC_other and changed-line counts low across the touched files.",
